<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK trades businesses - plumbers, electricians, builders, HVAC engineers, and specialist contractors - operate in a competitive market where reputation and efficiency determine success. The trades businesses thriving are the ones using technology to quote faster, manage jobs more efficiently, and deliver a professional customer experience. Yet many UK trades businesses still rely on a tangle of paper job sheets, spreadsheets for quoting, and evenings spent on admin that could be automated.</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf job management apps are built for the average trades business, not your specific trade. Generic packages don't understand the specific pricing structures of your trade, the way you manage van stock for your typical jobs, or the compliance requirements specific to your work - Gas Safe notifications for plumbers, Part P certifications for electricians, or building control sign-offs for builders. Quoting tools produce generic documents that don't reflect your branding or your specific service offering. Calendar and scheduling add-ons don't account for travel time between jobs or the specific skills and certifications each job requires. The result is trades business owners spending evenings on admin and losing jobs to competitors who quote faster.</p>
<p>We build custom software for UK trades businesses that streamlines the entire job lifecycle. From quoting and job management to van stock tracking and customer CRM, we build systems that fit your exact workflows. We understand trades - from the van to the customer's kitchen - and we build software that integrates with your existing accounting systems. Whether it's a bespoke quoting app that generates professional quotes on site and converts them to jobs with one tap, or a van stock system that tracks materials on each van and auto-reorders before you run out, bespoke software fits your trade.</p>
<p>Trades compliance carries real consequences. Gas Safe registrations, Part P electrical certifications, building control notifications, and H&S risk assessments all have specific record-keeping requirements. A missing Gas Safe notification or an unsigned electrical completion certificate isn't just a paperwork gap - it's a legal liability. Bespoke software generates compliance documentation automatically from job data, records certifications against specific jobs and customers, and sends automated reminders for annual inspections and service contracts - replacing paper systems that get lost in the van and are impossible to search during an audit.</p>
<p>A UK electrical contractor with 12 engineers was spending every evening generating quotes and invoices, with quotes often taking 24 hours to reach customers - losing jobs to faster competitors. We built a bespoke mobile app with on-site quoting, job management, photo documentation, and accounting integration. Quote turnaround dropped from 24 hours to 15 minutes, the business won 30% more jobs thanks to faster quoting, and evening admin was eliminated entirely. Van stock tracking reduced merchant trips by 40% and material waste by 15%.</p>
<p>Trades is a sector where bespoke software delivers clear, fast ROI. Every quote, every job, and every invoice generates data. The opportunity is building software that turns that data into faster quotes, efficient job management, and a professional customer experience that wins repeat business and referrals.</p>

